🛒 Bookshop — E-commerce Demo

A modern, full-stack e-commerce demo site featuring a product catalog, cart management, and secure payment processing using Stripe. Built with the MERN stack, Vite, and Bootstrap 5.

🛠️ Tech Stack

* MongoDB – NoSQL database for product and order storage
* Express.js – RESTful API backend
* React – Frontend with functional components and React Context for state management
* Node.js – Server runtime environment
* Vite – Lightning-fast frontend tooling
* Bootstrap 5 – Responsive layout and styling
* Stripe – Payment processing via Stripe Checkout API
* AdminJS – Admin interface for managing books and uploads

🔍 Features

* ✅ Product browsing with real-time data
* ✅ Dynamic cart management with add, update, and remove functionality
* ✅ Secure Stripe Checkout integration
* ✅ Order confirmation page
* ✅ Responsive design (mobile-friendly)
* ✅ Persistent cart using localStorage
* ✅ Clean React component structure
* ✅ Backend API for books and checkout
* ✅ AdminJS dashboard for book management

📂 Project Structure

🔹─ client               # React frontend (Vite)
│   🔹─ src
│   │   🔹─ components   # UI components (Navbar, ProductCard, etc.)
│   │   🔹─ pages        # Page-level components (Home, Product, Cart)
│   │   🔹─ context      # Cart context and state management
│   │   🔹─ api          # API requests to backend
│   │   └─ App.tsx
│   🔹─ public           # Static assets
│   🔹─ index.html
│   └─ vite.config.ts
🔹─ server               # Express backend
│   🔹─ models           # Mongoose schemas
│   🔹─ routes           # API routes for books, uploads, users
│   🔹─ controllers      # Route logic and Stripe integration
│   🔹─ admin             # AdminJS custom components
│   🔹─ uploads           # Uploaded book cover images
│   🔹─ index.mjs         # Express app entry point
│   └─ .env             # Backend environment variables
🔹─ package.json
└─ README.md

⚙️ Local Setup

Prerequisites:

* Node.js (v20+ recommended)
* MongoDB Atlas or local MongoDB instance
* Stripe account for API keys

Installation:

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/KatBreed/ecommerce-demo.git
cd ecommerce-demo

# Install server dependencies
cd server
npm install

# Install client dependencies
cd ../client
npm install
```

Environment Variables:

Server (server/.env)

```
MONGODB_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=your_stripe_secret_key
ADMIN_EMAIL=your_admin_email
ADMIN_PASSWORD=your_admin_password
COOKIE_SECRET=your_cookie_secret
BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
```

Client (client/.env)

```
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=your_stripe_public_key
```

🚀 Running the Project Locally

```bash
# Start the backend (from /server)
npm run dev

# Start the frontend (from /client)
npm run dev
```

Frontend: [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173)
Backend: [http://localhost:5000](http://localhost:5000)
Admin: [http://localhost:5000/admin](http://localhost:5000/admin)

🔑 Security Considerations

* All Stripe and AdminJS credentials are securely stored in backend environment variables.
* Use HTTPS for deployment to protect sensitive API keys and customer data.
* Use Stripe test mode for development. Switch to live keys only in production.

🔐 Deployment

This project is intended **for educational, personal, or portfolio use only. It is not intended for live, production deployment.** The product information and images used are for demonstration purposes and may be subject to copyright.

If you wish to deploy this project for learning purposes, recommended platforms include:

* **Frontend:** Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages
* **Backend:** Render, Heroku, DigitalOcean App Platform

When deploying for personal or educational purposes:

* Ensure **environment variables** are correctly set on your hosting provider.
* Configure the backend to allow **CORS** from your deployed frontend URL.
* Keep the project in **Stripe test mode** — do not use live keys.
* Always use **HTTPS** to protect data in transit.

⚠️ **Important:**
This project is not intended for commercial use or handling real customer transactions. Please do not use it in a live production environment.

📦 API Endpoints (Backend)

| Method | Endpoint                     | Description                      |
| ------ | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| GET    | /api/books                   | Fetch all books                  |
| GET    | /api/books/\:id              | Fetch single book                |
| GET    | /api/books/genre/\:genre     | Fetch books by genre             |
| POST   | /api/books                   | Create new book                  |
| POST   | /api/create-checkout-session | Initiate Stripe checkout session |
| POST   | /webhook                     | Stripe webhook endpoint          |
| GET    | /api/users (via userRoutes)  | User-related endpoints           |
| POST   | /api/upload                  | File upload endpoint             |

